# Scan the commit message itself.
#
# scan-pii.sh reads `git ls-files` and scan-text.sh reads a drafted file, so a
# commit message was the one outbound surface neither of them saw. A 2026-09-13
# audit found real household and contact names, a town, a postal code, a
# hostname and a LAN IP in eight published commit messages — including, with
# some irony, the messages of the commits that removed those same values from
# the files. A commit message is as public as the diff; it gets the same gate.
#
# $1 is the path to the message file, which is exactly what scan-text.sh takes.
bash scripts/scan-text.sh "$1"
